<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila's PHIBOR firmer as c. bank keeps rates.</title>
<headline>Manila's PHIBOR firmer as c. bank keeps rates.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-07-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippine interbank offered rates (PHIBOR) were firmer on Tuesday after the central bank kept its benchmark rates unchanged, traders said.</p>
<p>&quot;Yesterday's rate reduction was in anticipation of a further rate cut. Apparently, the central bank is not yet keen to cut rates further at this point,&quot; one trader said.</p>
<p>On Monday, PHIBOR slid in all maturities with short-term rates shedding two percentage points.</p>
<p>Another trader said the still volatile regional currencies had compelled some banks to keep a conservative stance and quote higher rates.  </p>
<p>Average rates quoted by 20 banks were:</p>
<p>			 JULY 22		 JULY 21</p>
<p>    1 W		24  7/8		 24  1/8</p>
<p>    2 W		23  1/4		 22  1/2</p>
<p>    1 M		20 11/16		19</p>
<p>    2 M		18  5/16		17  1/2</p>
<p>    3 M		16  7/8		 16</p>
<p>    6 M		15  3/4		 15  1/4</p>
<p>    12M		15  1/8		 14  3/4</p>
<p>    VAL		23-Jul		  22-Jul</p>
<p>-- Manila Newsroom (63 2) 841-8938 Fax 817-6267</p>
